# Traits

All reusable traits live under **`app/Traits/`** only. Do not add traits under `Http/Requests/.../Concerns`, `Models/Concerns`, or other layer folders.

## Layout

Group by area, mirroring existing folders:

| Folder | Examples |
|--------|----------|
| `app/Traits/Models/` | `WithStatus`, `WithNormalizedName` |
| `app/Traits/Requests/` | `WithUserVote` |
| `app/Traits/Tests/` | `WithUser` |
| `app/Traits/Enums/` | `WithValues` |
| `app/Traits/User/` | `WithBanned` |
| `app/Traits/Repository/` | `HasStatus` (legacy `Has*` — prefer `With*` for new traits) |

Pick the subfolder that matches the primary consumer (request, model, test, etc.).

## Naming

- **New traits:** prefer prefix **`With`** + descriptive suffix (`WithUserVote`, `WithRelatedSelects`).
- Legacy **`Has*`** traits remain as-is; do not rename without a dedicated refactor.
- One trait per file; class name = file name.

## Usage

```php
use App\Traits\Requests\WithUserVote;

class QuestionVoteUpdateRequest extends BaseFormRequest
{
    use WithUserVote;
}
```

Keep traits small and focused. No service calls, HTTP, or multi-step domain logic in traits (same spirit as [enums.mdc](enums.mdc)).
